Bundled data notes (not covered by the MIT code license above):

* data/adblock/* and data/seeds/* are *snapshots of public filter/proxy lists*
  fetched from GitHub (uBlock Origin uAssets — AGPL-3.0 with Commons Clause for
  the filter data; free proxy lists — MIT/Unlicense). They are shipped only as
  offline seeds so a fresh deploy still blocks ads before the first fetch.
  At runtime MirageVPN re-downloads the upstream lists; it does not redistribute
  them as its own work. Filter data is data, not code — treat its license
  obligations as applying to the snapshot files only, and delete them if that is
  not acceptable for your distribution.
* Nothing in this project is affiliated with, endorsed by, or a derivative of
  Ultraviolet (UV) or WISP. The transport/rewriter layers are original
  implementations that follow the same published ideas (URL token mapping,
  stream-multiplexed WebSocket tunneling), written from scratch, with no
  upstream source copied.
